// melee_duel.c - the MP melee DUEL, beat 1: one connecting hit that plays exactly like SP No Return (an SP-style 1v1 melee engagement).
// Spec: re/melee-duel-sp-spec.md sections 1-3, 9, 10 (NR log + gold-standard clip); SP pick rules / -hit windows: re/melee-dc/melee-dc.md.
// Opt-IN: t2r-melee-duel.txt next to the exe (re-read every 2 s). Without it every function here is a no-op and every hook line returns "not mine".
// Included after melee_qte.c in t2r-ext.c. Log prefix "DUEL:".
//
// Move table: mduel_moves.h (generated by tools/mv3/gen_duel_moves.py), one row per SP player swing of every melee set (fists, 1h blunt, 1h blade,
// 2h, switchblade) with its synced "-hit" pair, contact time, SP contact distance, combo window, next combo step and the swing clip's own vox / swish
// frames. The pairs are ctxdown.c CD_PAIRS rows of kind 7 ("md-<hit move>"), played by psync (paired.c) like the melee sequence's kind 6 rows.
// Beat 2 (this file): SCRIPTED DODGE, DODGE-COUNTER and the melee CAMERA inside the duel:
//  DODGE    the hit player's dodge press is judged by the SHARED-CLOCK RULE (below); the window of a duel swing closes at ITS contact on the victim's screen (mdu_window_end), the
//           press cuts a running -hit pair of ours (mdu_dodge_press: follow-up blows are dodgeable), the dodge itself is TLOU2's contextual dodge clip with its travel capped to
//           MDU_DODGE_CAP and the body turned back to the attacker (melee_dodge.c mdg_combat_play: no more "running out of the sequence"). The attacker's miss is its own swing clip's
//           slowed tail in place (mdu_miss_note: no stumble clip, no carry), the duel stays engaged (MDU_HOLD_MS) so the counter window is inside the sequence.
//  FAIRNESS the attacker decides contact at its contact frame with the presses that reached it (imm_until). The victim backs that with its own screen: a pair START that reaches it
//           while its i-frames cover the arrival (the press came before the contact showed on its screen) is refused with ABORT PS_AB_DODGED (paired.c, mdg_pair_dodged) and the
//           attacker plays the miss from that ABORT. So the dodger wins every press made before it SAW the contact (ties, latency included); log "DUEL: dodge ruling".
//  COUNTER  the press after a dodge is dcounter.c's connected SP counter (dc-* rows = abby-fist-dodge-back-attack / 1h dodge-back-attack pairs, 2 x fist damage, its own xcam
//           camera beat dc_cam); the facing gate is off in a duel, and dc starts / ends keep the duel engaged (mdu_note_dc).
//  CAMERA   melee_spcam.c: root cause of "the melee camera never enables" = melee_feel.c mfk_busy() counted psync_own() as busy, so every -hit pair (about 1 s per blow, the whole
//           duel) zeroed the framing weight + dropped the hit kicks; the duel pair is exempt now. New: the render camera is yawed toward the opponent (spm_yaw) on both screens.
// Later beats (parry, disarm, finisher) hook in at the places marked "HOOK:" - nothing of them is built here (parry: tools/ext/melee_duel_parry.c, another branch).
//
// Per blow (both screens):
//  ENGAGE   our swing starts (the engine picks the SP move: opener / sprint / left jab ...) with a standing enemy <= MDU_REACH m inside the soft-lock arc:
//           the two players are engaged (MSG_MEX op 5 ENGAGE). Both get the SP melee framing + fov (melee_spcam.c / meleefov.c keep it on for the duel).
//  SWING    attacker: facing locked onto the victim, the body warped every frame so the predicted root distance at the contact frame (tc_ms of the row,
//           SP's measured -hit switch) is the move's SP contact distance (0.3-2.4 m start). Effort vox + swish at the clip's own event frames, clamped to
//           SP's windows (-290..-155 / -170..-44 ms from contact). op 5 SWING tells the victim, whose screen plays the same cues on our puppet.
//  CONTACT  attacker decides: on the contact frame our swing is cancelled and psync starts <swing>-hit--abby|ellie on us + -hit--npc-* on the victim
//           on one align locator (dc_anchor: the victim half where the victim stands, turned so the authored attacker spot is us = the victim snaps to
//           face us in one frame, no position jump). The victim joins with a phase offset = the one-way latency (psync_begin_remote's skip).
//           Damage: the normal hit path (directhit_hook, fx lines skip themselves while the pair runs); the engine's own contact of this swing is dropped.
//           Sounds on both screens from the contact: victim pain +4, impact (+ blood) +35, second pain +40.
//  COMBO    the next press is accepted from the -hit move's combo window start (330 ms SP), an earlier press is buffered; the next step (the row's SP
//           next move) starts directly, our pair half blends out, the victim half plays on until the next contact replaces it. After the 4th hit
//           presses are dropped for MDU_GAP4_MS.
//  END      no blow for 1 s, partner > 3 m for 0.3 s, a lethal blow (the normal Melee Down takes it), either fighter down: END + 1.2 s cooldown on that pair.
//           A third player's hit on either fighter breaks the duel for both (op 5 BREAK + psync ABORT).
#include "mduel_moves.h"
static int DcArmedAt(uint64_t now);   // dcounter.c: the counter window is open now
#define MDU_DODGE_CAP 1.15f     // m: max travel of a dodge inside a duel (SP's in-melee dodge 0.38-1.12 m; was 0.55 with the confined clips; directional dodges travel)
#define MDU_HOLD_MS 2400        // after a dodge / miss the duel is held engaged this long: the counter window (600 ms) + the counter pair (~1.5 s)
// ps39: with one dodge clip at a time (melee_dodge.c) a dodger who pressed on the contact frame is free 60 + up to 990 ms later (the longest landing in rec37a);
// the attacker's next contact came 650 + 380 = 1030 ms after the missed one - no time left to dodge it. The lock is 800 ms [TUNING ps39]: next contact >= 1180 ms
// = that landing + SP's latest successful dodge start (133 ms before a contact). t2r-miss-lock-ps38.txt = 650.
static int MduMissLockMs(void)
{
    static int v = -1;
    static uint64_t at;
    uint64_t n = GetTickCount64();
    if (v < 0 || n - at > 3000) {
        at = n;
        v = GetFileAttributesA("t2r-miss-lock-ps38.txt") !=
            INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES;
    }
    return v ? 650 : 800;
}

